<title>USA: N.Y. Fed Press Briefing - October 24.</title>
<headline>N.Y. Fed Press Briefing - October 24.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve had no large one-day net misses in its reserve projections, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>As for the pattern of borrowing, all of the adjustment borrowing for the week was done by the small banks.</p>
<p>The high in natural float was a bit over $3.1 billion on Thursday, while the low was about $675 million on Monday.</p>
<p>Transportation float averaged a bit under $200 per day with the high on Thursday at about $500 million primarily due to fog in New York and other mid-Atlantic states.</p>
<p>-- Caryn Trokie 212-859-1678</p>
</text>
